        <div id="pint-ratings" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Pint Ratings and the 2019 DOE Change
          </h2>

          <p>
            If you have shopped for dehumidifiers before, the numbers may look smaller than you remember. In 2019 the Department of Energy changed the test that dehumidifier makers use to rate capacity. The old test ran at 80 degrees Fahrenheit and 60 percent relative humidity; the new one runs at 65 degrees and 60 percent, which is closer to real basements and homes. Colder air holds less water, so the same machine removes less of it, and the rating on the box dropped.
          </p>

          <p>
            The practical effect is that a unit once sold as 30 pints is now typically rated around 20 to 22 pints, a former 50-pint unit is now around 35, and a former 70-pint unit is now around 50. Toshiba's spec sheet for its 22-pint model makes this explicit, listing 22 pints a day alongside a previous rating of 30. Honeywell labels some of its units the same way, as a 30-pint model with a 20-pint 2019 DOE rating.
          </p>

          <p>
            This matters for bathrooms in two ways. First, when you compare a new model with an old review or a used unit, make sure both numbers use the same standard. Second, it puts the tiny Peltier units in perspective. Their ratings are usually quoted at 86 degrees and 80 percent humidity, conditions far kinder than either DOE test, so their real-world output in a 70-degree bathroom is lower still. A 9-ounce rating is a best case, not an everyday figure.
          </p>

          <p>
            For a full bathroom, a 20 to 22 pint unit under the 2019 standard is plenty. Bathrooms are small, and the moisture load comes in bursts. You do not need a 35 or 50 pint basement unit unless the bathroom is part of a damp basement you are drying as a whole, in which case one larger unit in the main space, with the bathroom door open, may do both jobs. Our <a href="/what-size-dehumidifier-for-basement/">dehumidifier sizing guide</a> covers that case.
          </p>

